    "title": "Five-Time Graded Stakes Winner Newgrange to Stand at Mountain View Farm in New York - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Past The Wire Staff ,\n1 days ago\nNewgrange under Victor Espinoza beats Baffert trainee of Newgate by a length in the GII San Pasqual at Santa Anita an. 27, 2024. (Ernie Belmonte/Past The Wire) GANSEVOORT, N.Y. — Mountain View Farm is pleased to announce that Newgrange, a five-time graded stakes-winning son of Violence with more than $1 million in earnings, will join its stallion roster in Gansevoort, New York. A debut winner at two who captured graded stakes at three, four and five, Newgrange offers breeders a combination of precocity, consistency and a pedigree that unites the influences of Medaglia d’Oro and Empire Maker.\nRead full article\nAdd to Preferred Sources",
    "summary": "By Past The Wire Staff , Newgrange under Victor Espinoza beats Baffert trainee of Newgate by a length in the GII San Pasqual at Santa Anita an. 27, 2024. (Ernie Belmonte/Past The Wire) GANSEVOORT, N.Y. — Mountain View Farm is pleased to announce that Newgrange, a five-time graded stakes-winning son of Violence with more than $1 million in earnings, will join its stallion roster in Gansevoort, New York.",
